    <recommendedCipherSuiteGuidelineCheck>
        <name>Given the foregoing considerations, implementation and deployment of the following cipher suites is RECOMMENDED.</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
            <result>TRUE</result>
        </condition>
        <versions>TLS12</versions>
        <recommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256</recommendedCipherSuites>
        <recommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384</recommendedCipherSuites>
        <recommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256</recommendedCipherSuites>
        <recommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384</recommendedCipherSuites>
    </recommendedCipherSuiteGuidelineCheck>
    <notRecommendedCipherSuiteGuidelineCheck>
        <name>A cipher suite that operates in CBC (cipher block chaining) mode (e.g., TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256) SHOULD NOT be used unless the encrypt_then_mac extension [RFC7366] is also successfully negotiated. This requirement applies to both client and server implementations.</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD_NOT</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <and>
                <condition>
                    <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
                    <result>TRUE</result>
                </condition>
                <condition>
                    <property>SUPPORTS_ENCRYPT_THEN_MAC</property>
                    <result>FALSE</result>
                </condition>
            </and>
        </condition>
        <versions>TLS12</versions>
        <notRecommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256</notRecommendedCipherSuites>
        <notRecommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384</notRecommendedCipherSuites>
        <notRecommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256</notRecommendedCipherSuites>
        <notRecommendedCipherSuites>TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384</notRecommendedCipherSuites>
    </notRecommendedCipherSuiteGuidelineCheck>
    <certificateCurveGuidelineCheck>
        <name>When using ECDSA signatures for authentication of TLS peers, it is RECOMMENDED that implementations use the NIST curve P-256.</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD</requirementLevel>
        <atLeastOneCertificateShallPass>false</atLeastOneCertificateShallPass>
        <recommendedNamedParameters>SECP256R1</recommendedNamedParameters>
    </certificateCurveGuidelineCheck>
    <notRecommendedCipherSuiteGuidelineCheck>
        <name>The previous version of the TLS recommendations [RFC7525] implicitly allowed [...] TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA. [...] As with other cipher suites that do not provide forward secrecy, implementations SHOULD NOT support this cipher suite.</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD_NOT</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
            <result>TRUE</result>
        </condition>
        <versions>TLS12</versions>
        <notRecommendedCipherSuites>TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA</notRecommendedCipherSuites>
    </notRecommendedCipherSuiteGuidelineCheck>
    <requiredExtensionGuidelineCheck>
        <name>Both clients and servers SHOULD include the "Supported Elliptic Curves Extension" [RFC8422].</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD</requirementLevel>
        <requiredExtensions>ELLIPTIC_CURVES</requiredExtensions>
    </requiredExtensionGuidelineCheck>
    <requiredNamedGroupsGuidelineCheck>
        <name>Clients and servers SHOULD support the NIST P‑256 (secp256r1) [RFC8422] and X25519 (x25519) [RFC7748] curves.</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD</requirementLevel>
        <requiredGroups>SECP256R1</requiredGroups>
        <requiredGroups>ECDH_X25519</requiredGroups>
        <onlyOneIsRequired>false</onlyOneIsRequired>
    </requiredNamedGroupsGuidelineCheck>
    <cipherSuiteFirstProposalGuidelineCheck>
        <name>Clients SHOULD include TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 as the first proposal to any server.</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
            <result>TRUE</result>
        </condition>
    </cipherSuiteFirstProposalGuidelineCheck>
    <ecPointFormatUncompressedOnlyCheck>
        <name>Note that [RFC8422] deprecates all but the uncompressed point format. Therefore, if the client sends an ec_point_formats extension, the ECPointFormatList MUST contain a single element, "uncompressed".</name>
        <requirementLevel>MUST</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
            <result>TRUE</result>
        </condition>
    </ecPointFormatUncompressedOnlyCheck>
    <keySizeCertGuidelineCheck>
        <name>4.5. Public Key Length</name>
        <requirementLevel>MUST</requirementLevel>
        <atLeastOneCertificateShallPass>false</atLeastOneCertificateShallPass>
        <minimumDsaKeyLength>0</minimumDsaKeyLength>
        <minimumRsaKeyLength>2048</minimumRsaKeyLength>
        <minimumEcKeyLength>224</minimumEcKeyLength>
        <minimumDhKeyLength>2048</minimumDhKeyLength>
    </keySizeCertGuidelineCheck>
    <recommendedHashAlgorithmsGuidelineCheck>
        <name>In addition, the use of the SHA-256 hash algorithm is RECOMMENDED and SHA-1 or MD5 MUST NOT be used [RFC9155] (for more details, see also [CAB-Baseline], for which the current version at the time of writing is 1.8.4).</name>
        <requirementLevel>SHOULD</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
            <result>TRUE</result>
        </condition>
        <recommendedAlgorithms>SHA256</recommendedAlgorithms>
    </recommendedHashAlgorithmsGuidelineCheck>
    <notRecommendedHashAlgorithmsGuidelineCheck>
        <name>In addition, the use of the SHA-256 hash algorithm is RECOMMENDED and SHA-1 or MD5 MUST NOT be used [RFC9155] (for more details, see also [CAB-Baseline], for which the current version at the time of writing is 1.8.4).</name>
        <requirementLevel>MUST_NOT</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
            <result>TRUE</result>
        </condition>
        <notRecommendedAlgorithms>SHA1</notRecommendedAlgorithms>
        <notRecommendedAlgorithms>MD5</notRecommendedAlgorithms>
    </notRecommendedHashAlgorithmsGuidelineCheck>
    <requiredExtensionGuidelineCheck>
        <name>Clients MUST indicate to servers that they request SHA-256 by using the "Signature Algorithms" extension defined in TLS 1.2. For TLS 1.3, the same requirement is already specified by [RFC8446].</name>
        <requirementLevel>MUST</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <or>
                <condition>
                    <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
                    <result>TRUE</result>
                </condition>
                <condition>
                    <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_3</property>
                    <result>TRUE</result>
                </condition>
            </or>
        </condition>
        <requiredExtensions>SIGNATURE_AND_HASH_ALGORITHMS</requiredExtensions>
    </requiredExtensionGuidelineCheck>
    <notRecommendedExtensionGuidelineCheck>
        <name>Implementations MUST NOT use the Truncated HMAC Extension, defined in Section 7 of [RFC6066].</name>
        <requirementLevel>MUST_NOT</requirementLevel>
        <condition>
            <property>SUPPORTS_TLS_1_2</property>
            <result>TRUE</result>
        </condition>
        <notRecommendedExtensions>TRUNCATED_HMAC</notRecommendedExtensions>
    </notRecommendedExtensionGuidelineCheck>
</guideline>
